Phase 3.1 Implementation Summary
=================================

CORE MODULES CHANGED
-------------------
1. aj/lease.py - LeaseManager class with acquire/renew/release/break_stale
   - File-backed leases with POSIX flock (non-POSIX in-process fallback)
   - Expired lease detection and break_stale requiring operator action
   - hold() context manager for safe lock acquisition

2. aj/journal.py - Journal append-only execution log
   - Event schema with event_id, task_id, operation_id, attempt_id
   - correlation_id, worker_id, lease_id, timestamp, schema_version
   - Metadata redaction via _redact()
   - file_lock-protected concurrent appends

3. aj/receipts.py - Per-attempt durable receipts
   - task_id, operation_id, attempt_id, worker_id, lease_id
   - capability_id, status, verification, started_at, completed_at
   - output, error (redacted), journal_event_ids

4. aj/idempotency.py - Persistent idempotency keys
   - Atomic duplicate submission via claim()
   - Returns existing task_id on duplicate key

5. aj/invariants.py - Read-only invariant checker
   - task invariants (status transitions, required fields)
   - lease invariants (active/expired/broken states)
   - receipt invariants (completeness, redaction)

6. aj/scheduler.py - Deterministic local scheduler
   - Bounded concurrency workers
   - Task claiming via lease acquisition
   - _run_one returns SchedulerResult

7. aj/retention.py - Non-destructive storage assessment
   - Assesses task/audit/memory/receipt sizes
   - Reports on storage health without mutation

8. aj/errors.py - Extended error types
   - LEASE_HELD, LEASE_EXPIRED, LEASE_OWNERSHIP
   - RETRY_UNSAFE, RECOVERY_REQUIRED (already existed, re-exported)

9. aj/task.py - Task state extensions
   - BLOCKED, DEAD_LETTER new states
   - depends_on: list of task_id dependencies
   - priority: int ranking
   - deadline: float epoch deadline
   - root_task_id: tree root identifier
   - schema_version: int for forward compat

10. aj/orchestrator.py - Routing through new infrastructure
    - Leases around execute/cancel/recover
    - Journal entries on all state changes
    - Receipt recording per attempt
    - Dependency checking (unsatisfied_dependencies)
    - Lineage computation (parent -> root -> children)
    - Dead-lettering (dead_letter method)
    - Resume from blocked/planned states via leases

11. aj/__main__.py - CLI extensions
    - cancel, retry, summary --rebuild --verify
    - config --check, diagnostics
    - export, import --dry-run, import, backup, backup --verify, recover
    - --json, --quiet, --verbose global flags
    - Exit code mapping: 0/1/2/3/4/5/6

12. README.md - Updated with Phase 3/3.1 semantics, exit codes, limitations

